{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/263797-echoes","id":263797,"title":"Echoes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-23T08:46:28-07:00","id":263797,"title":"Echoes","content":"Since I didn't see it anywhere else, I thought I'd make a thread to discuss ideas for new echoes a fetch can throw at the player. In particular I wanted to discuss very powerful echoes above level five. I know what Autumn Nightmares says on the subject....but not every changeling chooses to murder a fetch, and not every fetch is worthy of murder. Ergo there are bound to be SOME fetches who survive the Changeling's ascent above level five wyrd, and ergo there are Echoes they receive more powerful than those that have already been explored in the game setting. In my chronicle the king of the spring court has recently and mysteriously vanished from his post. Among other events that take place as a result of this event, the local Jack Ketch (the resident assassin of changeling fetches) has his eyes set on the king's fetch. Up until now he was bound to respect the prohibition to let the creature live as mandated by the spring king. Now that the king is gone our assassin no longer feels bound by that distasteful order. However, since the power of the creature is no doubt great and unknowable, Jack wants a little backup in taking it down. Hence where the PCs enter the picture.<br /> <br /> Please help me make this a fight they will remember. And please use this thread to discuss new and terrible forms of Fetch magic, even the &quot;normal&quot; variety of Echoes we see in the books below level five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T10:36:04-07:00","id":263915,"title":"","content":"Maybe some ability to duplicate a Kith, building off False Seeming? Or a way to &quot;attune&quot; to another Changeling, allowing it to treat that Changeling as if it were the one the Fetch is copying?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T17:21:06-07:00","id":264276,"title":"","content":"This exact thing played out in my game. At the end of a long, long campaign, one player was Wyrd 8 with a Fetch still active. The Fetch was generally considered a highly moral and a valuable ally, and its power grew well past where the game thinks it should have been able to get.<br /> <br /> I think I gave it the ability to mimic Contracts even when not in the player's presence, which given his Contract selection (mostly Elements and Stone) made it a seriously powerful creature. Other than that, I just loaded it with extra Echoes, letting it take two for every level above 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}